    description: "INV-fahub D facet. d_lang.py misbinds an unresolvable-receiver call (e.g. thing.exists()) to an arbitrary same-named internal def: exists(function) @0.85 (= 0.85 x 1.0 exact) for a top-level func. Misbind site: _resolve_and_emit_call_edge (d_lang.py:536-584), specifically the resolver.lookup at 563-567 emitting calls @ 0.85*conf at 568-577. Root cause is the WORST of the three: D does ZERO receiver/var-type tracking; the receiver is consulted only as an import-alias key (path_hint=import_aliases.get(receiver), 554-556), and — worse — `hints = imported_modules if not receiver else None` (562) DISABLES import-scope disambiguation the moment a receiver is present, so lookup does an unscoped global bare-name match. register_symbol (667-691) registers every func/method under its bare short name (691), seeding the exact-match.\n\nFIX (atomic, INV-nilud-conform): when a receiver is present but resolves to neither an import alias nor a tracked type, withhold the confident bare-name match and emit py.py's unresolved shape (calls, dst=d:external:0-0:{name}:unresolved, is_resolved=False, evidence_type=ast_call -> 0.40, meta={call_construct:method, +receiver_type_hint when typeable}). RECALL RECOVERY IS NOT OPTIONAL HERE: D must first grow at least minimal var->type tracking (from param types + `auto x = new T()` / typed decls) so it can attach a hint — otherwise ~100% of the funnel goes external with zero recovery (maximal dead-code FP spike). ADD 'd' to the inherited_calls Site-2 lang set for Step-1 direct.\n\nDISPOSITION DECISION (owner): if D var-type tracking is too large for one atomic PR, DEFER D entirely (out of the near-term INV-fahub build) rather than ship naked D suppression. Sequence LAST. Tests: linker template (lang=d) + d_lang.py producer test. Reproduces on current code @0.85 (verified 2026-07-17). Recall-regression severity: WORST."  # 4c09
    fields: {}  # 4c09
- op: discuss  # b859
  at: '2026-07-18T06:25:09Z'  # b859
  by: agent  # b859
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b859
  clock: 2  # b859
  nonce: b859  # b859
  message: "DEFERRED (owner decision 2026-07-18) after a read-only scope assessment. The standard atomic pattern (gate + type-threading + shared inherited_calls linker recovery) that closed the Scala (WI-bihit) and Swift (WI-votar) facets is INSUFFICIENT for D, for a D-specific reason: UFCS (Uniform Function Call Syntax). In D, 'thing.exists()' can mean EITHER a method on thing's type OR 'exists(thing)' — a free-function call. D's own model treats the receiver as a module prefix (_get_call_target_name_d: 'thing.exists()' -> (exists, 'thing')). The GATE is easy (a variable receiver that is not a known module -> suppress the misbind), but the shared linker's Site-2 recovery only resolves METHOD-on-type, NOT UFCS free-function resolution — so a legitimate 'thing.exists()' that is really 'exists(thing)' would be suppressed and CANNOT be recovered by the linker. Combined with (a) no existing var-type tracking (build from scratch) and (b) D's heavy 'auto' usage (many untyped-inference receivers -> no hint), naked D suppression would ship a large, UNRECOVERABLE recall regression on D's dominant call idiom (Agent-3's 'defer rather than ship naked' case). Doing D RIGHT requires UFCS-aware resolution — verify a free function's first-parameter type matches the receiver before binding — a D-specific resolver effort substantially larger than the Scala/Swift type-threading, arguably its own work item (candidate: a UFCS-aware Site in the inherited_calls linker, or an analyzer-side UFCS resolver). INV-fahub keeps its two clean facets (Scala + Swift, both merged); the D funnel (exists/startsWith/toString @0.85) stays open here, out of the near-term atomic build. Status kept todo_hard (deferred backlog, not near-term); re-scope to the UFCS-aware approach when picked up. Misbind sites unchanged: d_lang.py:536-584 (_resolve_and_emit_call_edge, resolver.lookup @0.85; 'hints=imported_modules if not receiver else None' at :562 disables import-scope disambiguation when a receiver is present)."  # b859
